# Directives dropped in here land inside this site's `tls` block. Empty by
# default, which is right for a server that gets its certificates from Let's
# Encrypt.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR: changing where certificates come from.
#
# A different certificate authority, or a local one during a trial:
#
#     ca https://acme.example.com/directory
#
# An address to be warned at when a certificate is about to expire:
#
#     email you@example.com
#
# A certificate you already hold, which is the answer for a domain behind
# Cloudflare's proxy. With the proxy on, the challenge Let's Encrypt sends is
# answered by Cloudflare rather than by this server, so issuance here fails.
# The two setups that work are a DNS-only (grey cloud) record, or the proxy on
# with Cloudflare set to Full (strict) and an Origin certificate mounted into
# this container:
#
#     tls /etc/caddy/certs/origin.pem /etc/caddy/certs/origin.key
#
# Flexible mode is not one of them: it sends traffic to this server in clear.
#
# This file is not decoration. With an empty directory Caddy logs
# "No files matching import glob pattern" on every start, which reads as a
# misconfiguration to whoever is tailing the logs for the first time.
